    LLM: "Bid conservatively â€” bidding 7 gives the same score as 8 or 9. Only bid higher than 7 if you're sure of 10+ tricks. Boom is high risk/reward.\n\nSince no suit is mentioned during bidding, coordinate trump choice carefully. If your partner bid before you, their lead will reveal their preferred suit. Don't overbid when partner has already committed.\n\nDefensive play against Boom bids is critical: winning a single trick gives your team 5 points. When opponents bid Boom, play your strongest card to the first trick. In Meetje, the dealer has an advantage knowing they'll choose trumps â€” bid 7 instead if you have a clear trump suit.",
